# ── the demo data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 150MB of ski-demo video, copied in by setup_demo.py rather than committed.
#
# Not a size decision. dev/ and sandbox/ are exactly the folders the editors
# WRITE to, so running the tools changes 106MB of files. Git keeps every
# version of every file forever and cannot pack video down, so each commit of
# a working state would add its full size again — permanently, since taking it
# back out means rewriting history.
#
# Both repos live on the same machine, so the data is one command away:
#     python3 setup_demo.py
Customers/**

# ── except the WORDS, which are small and are the thing worth keeping ────────
# Added 2026-08-28. `script.json` is the source of truth for a video's copy, and
# every one of them was git-tracked in Basic_E2E_Testing until the working files
# moved here — so a blanket `Customers/` would have quietly demoted four stores'
# scripts to disk-only, on the same day the folders they live in were rearranged.
#
# These are kilobytes of text and they carry what cost real money: the exact
# lines HeyGen was paid to speak, and which build each one produced. The video
# they describe stays out.
#
# The directory re-includes come FIRST and must: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a `!` on a file inside one is silently ignored.
!Customers/
!Customers/**/
Customers/**/z_History/**
!Customers/*/*/help-videos/**/*.json
!Customers/*/*/help-videos/**/*.md
!Customers/*/*/help-videos/**/*.txt
# A .vtt is SCRIPT, not footage — the same words as the script.json beside it,
# in the form an editor and a player can both read. Added 2026-09-09, when
# add-item's twelve-scene vtt was written and then silently not committed.
!Customers/*/*/help-videos/**/*.vtt
# vtt.html — the same words as a table, and the page Carson means by "show me
# the VTT". About 9KB. Kept in the two places it is a deliverable: beside a raw
# capture, and inside a release. NOT in dev/ or sandbox/, which the editors
# rewrite on every run — tracking a regenerated file there is pure churn, which
# is the whole reason Customers/** is excluded in the first place.
# ⚠ THE NAME IS <recipe>.vtt.html NOW, AND THIS PATTERN MISSED IT.
# Renamed 2026-09-14 so eight of these in eight tabs can be told apart. These
# two lines still said plainly `vtt.html`, so every renamed page fell back to
# the blanket `Customers/**` exclusion and silently stopped being tracked —
# checked with `git check-ignore`. Match the suffix, not the whole basename.
# ⚠ AND THE PATTERN MUST NOT NAME THE STAGE FOLDER EITHER. These two lines
# said `raw_mp4/` and `videos/`, and BOTH names are gone: ski-demo split into
# BCP_raw_mp4/UI_raw_mp4 and renamed videos/ to development_videos/ on
# 2026-09-15, and bike-demo, canoe-demo and alpine-sports were refactored to
# match the same day. So all TEN pages on disk fell back to the blanket
# `Customers/**` exclusion and stopped being tracked — the identical silent
# failure the note above describes, from a different direction.
#
# So: un-ignore the page ANYWHERE under help-videos, then put back the two
# places it must not be tracked. `dev/` and `sandbox/` are rewritten by the
# editors on every run, and a regenerated tracked file is pure churn.
!Customers/*/*/help-videos/**/*vtt.html
Customers/*/*/help-videos/**/dev/**/*vtt.html
Customers/*/*/help-videos/**/sandbox/**/*vtt.html
# ...but NOT the editable artifact page. `<recipe>.vtt.artifact.html` is built
# on demand by Recorder/scripts/vtt_artifact.py, published straight to an
# artifact, and stale the moment a line is edited. There is no version of it
# worth keeping, and a tracked copy would disagree with the live page.
Customers/*/*/help-videos/**/*.vtt.artifact.html
!Customers/*/*/help-videos/**/.gitkeep
# The cut plan's contact sheet — 65 KB, and the tool tells you to look at it
# before cutting. It was tracked in Basic_E2E_Testing for the same reason;
# keep it, or the boundaries.json beside it names frames nobody can see.
!Customers/*/*/help-videos/**/work/boundaries.png
# ...but not these. `.render_jobs.json` holds live HeyGen job ids, and a frame
# map is regenerable diagnostics that runs to thousands of lines.
Customers/**/.render_jobs.json
Customers/**/cache/**

# EVERY extracted-frame cache, under one folder since 2026-09-04 — there were
# five at the repo root and Carson did not want to scroll past them:
#   cache/_shared/                the old 8842 server and Frame Blender
#   cache/mp4-splitter/           |
#   cache/segment-avatar-editor/  | one per standalone editor, so one tool's
#   cache/avatar-editor/          | Clear can never throw away another's frames
#   cache/go/                     the next-gen Go server's own
#   cache/ruff/                   ruff's, via cache-dir in pyproject.toml
cache/

# Run logs: the record of one machine's work, not source.
logs/*.log
tests/log_reports/*.log

# Per-editor test output (2026-09-03 split) — one folder per editor, a
# .log (the full transcript) and a .txt (the pass/fail report) per run,
# same base filename. .gitkeep keeps the 4 folders themselves in git even
# with nothing run yet.
tests/avatar_editor/*.log
tests/avatar_editor/*.txt
tests/frame_blender/*.log
tests/frame_blender/*.txt
tests/mp4_splitter/*.log
tests/mp4_splitter/*.txt
tests/segment_avatar_editor/*.log
tests/segment_avatar_editor/*.txt
tests/editor_base/*.log
tests/editor_base/*.txt
!tests/*/.gitkeep

# Generation archives — dev/, sandbox/ and video/ each keep their previous
# batch. Under Customers/ and so already ignored, but named here because the
# rule is about what they ARE, not where they sit.
**/z_History/
# Same reasoning, added 2026-08-29 for the two other generation-snapshot
# folders this project now makes: Backup Scenes' own archive (holds a copy
# of script.json alongside the scene folders, which the re-includes above
# would otherwise let back in), and an ad-hoc personal backup folder.
**/1000_archive/
**/sandbox_editor_bkup/

# ── secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The HeyGen key. Every render against it is a real charge, so this must never
# be committed — the rule is written BEFORE the file is created, not after.
.env.local
**/.env.local
.env

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# ── the test suites' source footage — the RULE is committed, the bytes are not ─
# Three clips, 3.7 MB, that every one of tests/' six suites builds its store
# from. They follow this repo's no-video-in-git rule like everything else, so
# only the README travels. See tests/_fixture_source/README.md for why they
# live there and what happens if they go missing.
Video-Editors/tests/_fixture_source/*
!Video-Editors/tests/_fixture_source/README.md

# ── MUX-Management/ — the video DELIVERY side, moved in from Basic_E2E_Testing ─
# 2026-09-05. Block what is DANGEROUS or LARGE; track everything else.
#
# The first version of this rule excluded the whole folder and re-included only
# .md/.txt. That would have silently DROPPED VSCode_Mux_Ex's Go + React source
# — a real prototype, tracked in the other repo until today — turning a move
# into a deletion of its history. Caught before the commit; do not narrow this
# back to a docs-only allowlist.
#
# ⚠ Live MUX API tokens and .pem SIGNING KEYS live under Help_Videos/MUX/.
# These rules are what stop them being committed.
MUX-Management/**/*.env
MUX-Management/**/*.env.*
!MUX-Management/**/*.env.example
MUX-Management/**/*.pem
MUX-Management/**/*.key
MUX-Management/**/*secret*
MUX-Management/**/*token*
MUX-Management/**/*signing-key*
# Media: the renders are hundreds of MB and are regenerable output.
MUX-Management/**/*.mp4
MUX-Management/**/*.webm
MUX-Management/**/*.mov
MUX-Management/**/*.mp3
MUX-Management/**/*.wav
MUX-Management/**/*.png
MUX-Management/**/*.jpg
MUX-Management/**/node_modules/

# sae_vtt_sync.py records (Basic_E2E_Testing): file sizes + times on THIS machine,
# meaningless anywhere else. One per sandbox scene.
**/sandbox/**/.sync.json
